phy: sunxi-cadence-combophy: gate the software HPD on the DP_STATUS HPD bit

0104 added typec-dp-no-hpd for boards like the Cubie A7S that route no usable
physical HPD, publishing the connection state through the DP extcon instead.
It derived that state from the Alt Mode state alone:

	hpd_state = state == TYPEC_DP_STATE_C || ... || TYPEC_DP_STATE_F;

Being in a DP Alt Mode state means the mux is pointed at DP. It does not mean
a sink is ready to answer. The sink reports that separately over CC in the
DP_STATUS HPD bit, which the phy switcher already folds into bit 6 of the
submode - the value this then overwrote.

The two are not simultaneous. On the dock tested here the mux reaches
STATE_DP_D with DP_STATUS 0x1a (HPD low) and the sink only asserts HPD ~230ms
later at 0x9a. Publishing "connected" on the earlier event makes the eDP
driver read DPCD from a sink that is not listening yet; AUX times out, DPCD is
never parsed, and the link is trained from stale devicetree lane parameters.

Require both conditions instead of overriding one with the other. This is the
same connection authority mainline uses for DP alt mode, and it closes the
race at its source rather than papering over it with a retry.

Note this makes a sink that never sets DP_STATUS HPD stay disconnected, which
is the correct behaviour but is stricter than 0104 was.

Signed-off-by: Paul Goldsmith <goldfish.paul@gmail.com>
---
--- a/bsp/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c
@@ -2504,17 +2504,31 @@
 		}
 
 		/*
-		 * Cubie A7S Type-C DP has no usable physical HPD input.  Its Type-C
-		 * controller has already established the DP Alt-Mode state, which is
-		 * the connection authority for this opt-in board.  Do not alter the
-		 * hardware HPD signal or controller registers; only publish the
-		 * software connection state through the existing DP extcon.
+		 * Cubie A7S Type-C DP has no usable physical HPD input, so the
+		 * connection state has to be published in software through the DP
+		 * extcon rather than read off a pin. Never touch the hardware HPD
+		 * signal or the controller HPD registers on such a board.
+		 *
+		 * Being in a DP Alt Mode state is necessary for that but not
+		 * sufficient: it only says the mux is pointed at DP, not that a
+		 * sink is ready to answer. The sink reports readiness over CC in
+		 * the DP_STATUS HPD bit, which the switcher folds into bit 6 of
+		 * the submode, so require both.
+		 *
+		 * Treating the Alt Mode state alone as "connected" - which is what
+		 * this did - fires the extcon the instant the mux flips, typically
+		 * a couple of hundred milliseconds before the sink asserts HPD
+		 * (DP_STATUS 0x1a -> 0x9a on the dock tested here). The eDP driver
+		 * takes that as a plug event and immediately reads DPCD from a sink
+		 * that is not listening yet; AUX times out, DPCD is never parsed,
+		 * and the link is then trained from stale devicetree lane
+		 * parameters. Gating on HPD closes that race at its source.
 		 */
 		if (sunxi_cphy->typec_dp_no_hpd)
-			hpd_state = state == TYPEC_DP_STATE_C ||
-				    state == TYPEC_DP_STATE_D ||
-				    state == TYPEC_DP_STATE_E ||
-				    state == TYPEC_DP_STATE_F;
+			hpd_state = hpd_state && (state == TYPEC_DP_STATE_C ||
+						  state == TYPEC_DP_STATE_D ||
+						  state == TYPEC_DP_STATE_E ||
+						  state == TYPEC_DP_STATE_F);
 
 		if (combo0->hpd_state != hpd_state) {
 			if (sunxi_cphy->extcon)
